# Facts of the PrefetchCache gates in middleware_pipeline.py. prefetchServe answers the
# cache-above-circuit read (duplicated verbatim at the pre-circuit check and inside
# _pre_tcp_guards -- one source of truth instead of two copies that could drift).
# prefetchFire answers whether _maybe_prefetch_background may even look up GATE_PRIORS
# for this write (the GATE_PRIORS dispatch table itself stays native: a per-cmd predicted-read
# builder, not a boolean ladder).
CONTRACT unitymcp.prefetch
COVERAGE declared-scope
MODULE prefetch_facts
FACT pf.cacheConfigured bool
FACT pf.cmdCacheable bool
FACT pf.scenarioUncertain bool
FACT pf.cmdIsWrite bool
FACT pf.cmdSceneNeutral bool
INPUT prefetchServe pf.cacheConfigured pf.cmdCacheable pf.scenarioUncertain
INPUT prefetchFire pf.cacheConfigured pf.scenarioUncertain pf.cmdIsWrite pf.cmdSceneNeutral
